            "review_title": "Review at Okachan Shokudo",
            "review_text": "Edokko\nZushi, Japan684 contributions\n0\nExquisite soup curry made by a general who has been in Japan for 9 years\nJun 2025 • Business\nOn June 10, 2025, I visited with a colleague from the company I was traveling with.\nMy colleague happened to find it, so I went out for my first Japanese meal in a while. The place was in a back alley, which was a bit suspicious, but I was brave enough to enter because it was run by a Japanese. Even though it was shortly before the store opened, they were willing to let me in.\nWe had soup curry, which other people have praised. I made pork medium spicy (middle spiciness) because you can choose ingredients, spiciness and toppings. The pork was simmered in simmered cubes, and the curry was moderately spicy, with beer progressing.\nThe store was decorated with photos and trophies showing the baseball team's success in Hanoi, and the customers also had baseball teammates visiting the store, making the store feel at home.\nNext time, I would like to try other menu. It seems to be a place of healing during a long business trip to Hanoi.\nRead more\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten June 18, 2025",
